<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-26987] Fix control.sh --kill compute command permissions check and authorization errors propagation</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-26987</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The control.sh --kill compute command ignores any errors that occur during its execution.&lt;br/&gt;
For example, control.sh --kill compute may fail if the user does not have sufficient privileges, but currently, in this case, the command completes with success status and no sign of errors.&lt;br/&gt;
see org.apache.ignite.internal.management.kill.ComputeCancelSessionTask#reduce0&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; It also requires excess ADMIN_OPS permission along with TASK_CANCEL.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
